# Registry block media (images & video)

Use this when a block needs bundled raster images (PNG, JPG, WebP) or video (MP4, WebM). Most blocks (navbars, SVG-only sections, etc.) do not need this.

## Consumer install (shadcn add)

One command for consumers:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add "https://uiception.com/r/<block-id>.json"
npm run dev
```

`shadcn build` + `post-registry-build.mjs`:

1. Strip binary `content` from `public/r/*.json` media entries (shadcn cannot embed PNG/MP4 as UTF-8).
2. Set `meta.installUrl` on those entries (metadata only — **the shadcn CLI does not read this**).
3. Inject a text `registry:file` at `lib/uiception-media/pending/<block-id>.json` listing `{ target, url }` pairs.
4. Add registry dependency `https://uiception.com/r/uiception-media-fetch.json`, which installs `instrumentation.ts` and `lib/uiception-media/fetch-uiception-media.mjs`.

On first `next dev` or `next build`, instrumentation reads the pending manifests and downloads missing files into `public/images/blocks/<block-id>/` or `public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/`.

Tests in `registry-shadcn-media-install.test.ts` guard this flow.

## Where assets live

**Images**

```
public/images/blocks/<block-id>/
  hero-section-v8-bg.png
  avatar_1.png
```

**Video**

```
public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/
  screen-demo.mp4
```
